  "application_type_full": "Householder planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed hip-to-gable roof extension above the main house, including the alterations to the roof above the existing two-storey side extension, would disrupt the symmetry and balanced appearance of the semi-detached pair, resulting in an incongruous and visually harmful form of development. Furthermore, the proposed rear dormer, by reason of its excessive scale and improper design, would form a dominant, bulky and unbalanced addition that would detract from the proportions and character of the dwelling and the wider roofscape. As such, the proposal would fail to respect the character and appearance of the host property and surrounding area, contrary to Policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 of the Hounslow Local Plan and the Residential Extension Guidelines (Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD)."
  ],
